<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc235450419" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 1 — Image placed inside an admonition</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a &lt;div class="warning"&gt; element where the author has inserted an &lt;img&gt; element — for</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>warning</keyword>
        <keyword>element</keyword>
        <keyword>inside</keyword>
        <keyword>admonition</keyword>
        <keyword>image</keyword>
        <keyword>Image</keyword>
        <indexterm>warning</indexterm>
        <indexterm>element</indexterm>
        <indexterm>inside</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
         <p>Consider a <codeph>&lt;div class="warning"&gt;</codeph> element where the author has inserted an <codeph>&lt;img&gt;</codeph> element — for example, a photograph of a hazardous component — directly inside the warning content.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Image placed inside admonition</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;div class="warning">
  &lt;p>
    Do not touch the marked components.
    &lt;img ... />
  &lt;/p>
&lt;/div></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;note type="warning">
  Do not touch the marked components.
  &lt;fig id="...">
    &lt;image placement="break" href="media/hazard_component.png" id="image_s1v_ymr_pjc">
      &lt;alt>an image&lt;/alt>
    &lt;/image>
  &lt;/fig>
&lt;/note></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p><b>Result:</b> The converter extracts the <codeph>&lt;img&gt;</codeph> element and maps it to a DITA <codeph>&lt;fig&gt;</codeph> element containing <codeph>&lt;image placement="break"/&gt;</codeph>. The <codeph>&lt;note&gt;</codeph> element wraps both the warning text and the <codeph>&lt;fig&gt;</codeph> as a single block-level admonition.</p>
         </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
